WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.780
Since 1983, one US dollar has
bought about 7.80 Hong Kong dollars.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.300
The euro floats: markets set its price.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.830
The Hong Kong dollar has
been held still for decades.

4
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.870
In September 1992, Britain
raised interest rates from 10

5
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.410
to 12 per cent in one day to hold

6
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.950
the pound in place.

7
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.220
That evening, it gave up.

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.560
So can a country choose
the price of its own money,

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.640
and what does it cost to try?

10
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.770
In this mission, you'll meet
three exchange rate systems:

11
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.460
floating, fixed and managed.

12
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.340
Then you'll defend a peg
yourself in the graph lab,

13
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.710
and watch how long the reserves last.

14
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.680
Your mission: find out what
it really takes to hold

15
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.320
a currency's price still.
